assistant: Subject: Read unit_amount when vendor omits price
Vendor API version 2026-10-01 changed the product response: the unit price now comes in `unit_amount` instead of `price`, even though the published OpenAPI spec still only lists `price`. `get_product` only read `p.price ?? null`, so for new-version responses it returned `price: null` while the vendor had actually sent 1199. The fix adds `unit_amount` to the `VendorProduct` type and maps `price` from `p.price ?? p.unit_amount ?? null`. Old-version responses that send `price` still produce exactly the same output, and `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test` all pass. I copied `unit_amount` over as-is, in dollars: the recorded call shows the same 1199 the v1 fixture returned as `price`, and the spec says nothing about units. `search_products` also reads `price`, so it may have the same problem under the new version, but I left it unchanged because no new-version response for it was available to check against.

